      "message": "VoIP Calls: Check whether Q.931 calls are complete\n\nProcess the queue of VoIP calls backwards from the tail, since the most\nrecent calls are added to the end. (This should probably be done\nelsewhere in the function.) If the most recent matching call (same CRV,\netc.) is active, or the new message type is for a call ending, then\nuse that call. Else, the newly tapped message creates a new call.\n\nFix #19653\n",
